<h1>TActiveDatePicker</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1.3" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveDatePicker" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveDatePicker</tt> is the active control counterpart of
<a href="?page=Controls.DatePicker">TDatePicker</a>. It offers the same calendar and input
modes, and it reaches the server through a callback when the selected date changes.
<tt>AutoPostBack</tt> defaults to true here, unlike on the ordinary control.
</p>

<h2>Events</h2>

<p class="block-content">
Changing the date raises <tt>OnTextChanged</tt> first, inherited from the text box the
control is built on, and <tt>OnCallback</tt> second.
</p>

<h2>Updating the date during a callback</h2>

<p class="block-content">
Assigning <tt>Text</tt> writes the new date into the field in the browser. This one update
carries an extra condition beyond <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>: the page must already have loaded
its post data. A date assigned earlier than that is kept on the server and never sent, so
write it from <tt>OnLoad</tt> or from the callback handler rather than from
<tt>OnInit</tt>.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
Under the <tt>DropDownList</tt> input mode the control shows three select elements rather
than a text field. Assigning <tt>Text</tt> then sets the day, the month, and the year
lists as well, so the three stay in step with the value.
</p>

